 Building on the hackathon outputs and the trends above, we highlight several promising directions for BO in chemistry and materials discovery. \emph{Autonomous and self-driving laboratories} are a natural home for BO, closing the loop between algorithmic suggestion and automated experimentation~\cite{tom_self-driving_2024, abolhasani_rise_2023}. \emph{Multi-fidelity optimization} that fuses cheap simulations or proxy measurements with expensive experiments can substantially reduce cost, provided its assumptions are handled carefully~\cite{sabanza-gil_best_2025, judge_applying_2024}. \emph{Uncertainty-aware experimental planning} and active learning under design constraints can make campaigns more sample-efficient and trustworthy~\cite{low_evolution_2024}.
 
-The large share of hackathon projects that already incorporated language models points to \emph{foundation-model- and LLM-assisted BO} as a particularly active frontier for design-space specification, prior construction, and warm-starting; reported evidence on whether LLM-based surrogates and priors outperform strong classical baselines is mixed, and benchmarking such hybrids fairly (separating genuine generalization from memorized results) is itself an open problem~\cite{kristiadi_sober_2024, rankovic_gollum_2025}. Other opportunities include \emph{preference-based and human-in-the-loop BO} for subjective or hard-to-quantify objectives~\cite{adachi_looping_2024, deneault_preferential_2025}; \emph{multi-objective materials design} with scalable hypervolume-based acquisitions~\cite{ament_unexpected_2023}; \emph{robust BO under noisy experimental data}~\cite{aldeghi_golem_2021, altamirano_robust_2023}; \emph{community benchmark development} to enable reproducible, apples-to-apples comparisons~\cite{liang_benchmarking_2021, felton_summit_2021}; use of agents to redefine search spaces mid-campaign \cite{muller_la_agente_optima_2026}; and \emph{domain-specific, deployment-ready BO tools} for synthesis and processing optimization that meet experimentalists where they work, including a growing set of graphical and web-based BO interfaces that remove coding barriers~\cite{durholt_bofire_2024, fitzner_baybe_2022, ishii_boxvia_2022, torres_multi-objective_2022, tamura_nims-os_2023}. Collectively, these directions echo the broader perspective that Bayesian methods are a core component of the autonomous materials-discovery toolkit~\cite{arroyave_perspective_2022}.
